授業科目の目的・目標・履修条件について.授業科目の目的（英語）:
This course intends to
1. provide students with a comprehensive understanding of complex numbers and functions, emphasizing their relevance in engineering contexts;
2. to equip them with the ability to apply complex analysis techniques to solve practical engineering problems;
3. to ensure mastery of core concepts and theorems in complex analysis, including continuity, differentiability, and the Residue Theorem;
4. to foster critical thinking and problem-solving skills through challenging engineering scenarios that require the application of complex analysis principles; and
5. to prepare students for advanced coursework in engineering fields where complex analysis is a fundamental tool, emphasizing its interdisciplinary applicability
